			<Item class="Script" referent="RBX2361">
				<Properties>
					<bool name="Disabled">true</bool>
					<Content name="LinkedSource"><null></null></Content>
					<string name="Name">Readme</string>
					<ProtectedString name="Source">--[[

I would like to point out that the original script was from BlueTaslem.
It was modifed by blobbyblob, and if you want your own channel to be
distributed in the main tv, blobbyblob is the one to PM.

If you wish to modify your channels, do it with the script called &quot;channels&quot;

You don&apos;t have to PM blobbyblob to insert your channels in your personal TV.
&quot;Inserting Your Own Channel&quot; explains how to do this.

Verbal Commands:

set the channel:
channel/[channel number]

insert a channel with default settings:
insert/[Place ID]

insert a channel with preset settings:
insertchannel/[Place Table]

remove a channel:
remove/[Channel Number]</ProtectedString>
				</Properties>
				<Item class="Script" referent="RBX2362">
					<Properties>
						<bool name="Disabled">true</bool>
						<Content name="LinkedSource"><null></null></Content>
						<string name="Name">ResizeYourTV!</string>
						<ProtectedString name="Source">--[[

TV too large?

You will have to PM blobbyblob. A recent update disabled the command that used
to be used to resize the TV. Now, the only way would be to resize it in an old version
of roblox. PM me and tell me the X and Y sizes that your TV needs to fit in.
</ProtectedString>
					</Properties>
				</Item>
				<Item class="Script" referent="RBX2363">
					<Properties>
						<bool name="Disabled">true</bool>
						<Content name="LinkedSource"><null></null></Content>
						<string name="Name">Inserting Your Own Channel</string>
						<ProtectedString name="Source">--[[

NOTE: All placeIDs only consist of the last numbers. Do not include the entire link. The same goes with Frames.

Here is the guide to inserting your own channel into your personal TV.

If you want a static channel, type:
{PlaceID,&quot;ChannelName&quot;,&quot;PlayerName&quot;,CharacterVisible}

PlaceID - A number. The numbers at the end of your place&apos;s URL
ChannelName - a string - what you call your channel. Don&apos;t forget the quotes!
PlayerName - a string - what your name is. Don&apos;t forget the quotes!
CharacterVisible - a bool. Does your character&apos;s picture show up when that channel is on?

If you want a dynamic channel, the layout is:
{SplashScreen,&quot;ChannelName&quot;,&quot;PlayerName&quot;,CharacterVisible,FlipTime,Frame1,Frame2,Frame3,etc.}

SplashScreen - A number. The numbers at the end of your place&apos;s URL. This screen shows for 5 seconds before going to Frame1
ChannelName - a string - what you call your channel. Don&apos;t forget the quotes!
PlayerName - a string - what your name is. Don&apos;t forget the quotes!
CharacterVisible - a bool. Does your character&apos;s picture show up when that channel is on?
FlipTime - a number. The amount of time between each Frame.
Frame1, Frame2, Frame3, etc. - The different frames in your animation.


</ProtectedString>
					</Properties>
				</Item>
				<Item class="Script" referent="RBX2364">
					<Properties>
						<bool name="Disabled">true</bool>
						<Content name="LinkedSource"><null></null></Content>
						<string name="Name">Version History</string>
						<ProtectedString name="Source">--[[

v2.0.0
Basic version - played all media

v2.0.1
Simple bug fixes

v2.1.0
Added Chat script to allow people to insert channels in-game (&quot;insert/[Place ID]&quot;)

v2.1.1
Bug Fixes.

v2.1.2
Animation Bugs Fixed.

v2.1.3
Included script to resize the TV.

v2.1.4
Security Fix. This is an important update for your game so people cannot cheat using scripts.

</ProtectedString>
					</Properties>
				</Item>
			</Item>
